ected security, privacy, and GDPR pages into one legal-trust family.\",\n    \"securityCenter.changelog.3\": \"Made public security language more operational and less generic.\",\n    \"securityCenter.changelog.title\": \"What changed in this security experience\",\n    \"securityCenter.contact.body\": \"If you need help evaluating product security, trust posture, or incident-readiness claims, contact our support workflow and we will route the request appropriately.\",\n    \"securityCenter.contact.privacy\": \"Privacy and GDPR pages remain linked for rights-based follow-up\",\n    \"securityCenter.contact.status\": \"Operational trust also depends on monitoring and recovery continuity\",\n    \"securityCenter.contact.support\": \"Help & Support workspace\",\n    \"securityCenter.contact.title\": \"Security, trust, or platform-risk questions\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.encryption.body\": \"Transport, storage, and token handling protections support sensitive workflows.\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.encryption.title\": \"Encryption layers\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.identity.body\": \"Authentication, route-access, and account-state controls work together.\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.identity.title\": \"Identity & access\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.operations.body\": \"Monitoring, response, and recovery practices reinforce user trust.\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.operations.title\": \"Operational defense\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.privacy.body\": \"Security remains connected to privacy rights, legal notice, and data control flows.\",\n    \"securityCenter.fact.privacy.title\": \"Trust continuity\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.badge\": \"SECURITY TRUST CENTER\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.cta.contact\": \"Contact Security & Support\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.cta.privacy\": \"Review Privacy Commitments\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.imageAlt\": \"Abstract security infrastructure background\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.meta.linkage\": \"Linked to Privacy and GDPR trust surfaces\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.meta.response\": \"Operational incident workflows support rapid detection and recovery\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.meta.updated\": \"Last updated: March 20, 2026\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.subtitle\": \"This page turns platform security, reliability, incident readiness, and trust controls into a readable product-grade security experience.\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.title\": \"Security posture that users can understand before they trust us with work.\",\n    \"securityCenter.hero.version\": \"Version 2026.2\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.compliance.p1\": \"Our security posture connects to privacy, GDPR, account protection, and legal notice workflows so users are not forced to treat these as disconnected promises.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.compliance.p2\": \"This means public trust pages, privacy request actions, and policy update communications can reinforce one another instead of drifting apart over time.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.compliance.summary\": \"Security posture is strongest when privacy rights, legal transparency, and operational controls stay connected.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.compliance.title\": \"Compliance, privacy, and user controls\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.encryption.p1\": \"We use layered controls such as transport encryption, at-rest protection, role-based access, session controls, and provider-backed authentication flows to reduce unauthorized access risk.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.encryption.p2\": \"Authentication and access policy are linked to account state, entitlement controls, and security workflows rather than isolated login-only logic.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.encryption.summary\": \"Core protections for credentials, sessions, transport, storage, and privileged access.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.encryption.title\": \"Encryption, authentication, and access control\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.focus\": \"Pin section\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.b1\": \"Operational monitoring and alerting support early issue detection\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.b2\": \"Incident workflows support containment, recovery, and review\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.b3\": \"Security and privacy surfaces remain linked for user trust continuity\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.p1\": \"Monitoring, alerting, performance checks, route-health controls, and audit visibility all contribute to our security posture. Security is linked to reliability because silent product failure is also a trust issue.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.p2\": \"When incidents happen, we aim for documented response, operational containment, and transparent recovery practices rather than vague blanket assurances.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.summary\": \"We use layered monitoring and operational response patterns to detect issues and recover quickly.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.operations.title\": \"Monitoring, incident response, and platform operations\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.posture.b1\": \"Security posture is tied to identity, route access, plan state, and operational monitoring\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.posture.b2\": \"Public trust signals remain connected to privacy and GDPR rights surfaces\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.posture.b3\": \"Controls are intended to be legible to both individuals and compliance reviewers\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.posture.p1\": \"RealAICoach is built for users and teams who need visible guardrails around access, billing, privacy, and operational trust. Security is treated as a product layer, not an afterthought hidden in vendor jargon.\",\n    \"securityCenter.section.posture.p2\": \"Our public security page is designed to help users evaluate our approach before they become paid users, and to support lightweight due-diligence conversations without requiring an enterprise sales workflow first.\",\n   